              "uri": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHUIY-2bN1B25BSJikpgsRoawQWptn3CLlGHpc3nVxHwKqbW8ot40FpKO3ykt51EzcywHxlYVL1ZX21X7jG7x5fE8QICN5P2gQYpfD5dkQUlYZEeejSTM7wuM1cVub9OgVdmbfpMLbkkYLRcsI4Vw=="
            }
          },
          {
            "image": null,
            "maps": null,
            "retrieved_context": null,
            "web": {
              "domain": null,
              "title": "thomsonreuters.com",
              "uri": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGvo-1MJ64JafJ5qYxRG6SdcEImIC2kxGPGB3HdvT7DzTo_rENDpBaMxtY3i2PFzRyoWBVIbkAyk4ZtIbavzoZe6A6jn22fXPjB1--OqNf01HP_390RoKn5m5ccuiFwOqz5TZ2u_ngG2CwyQrWYMr2CF8UjHh57XeWfpyZMfiEFoK0ZbR0K7psu4ig7sdGUEZQ8ml6Xq-fpEEFQEK0xzGI="
            }
          }
        ],
        "grounding_supports": [
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              0,
              1,
              2,
              3,
              4,
              5,
              6
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 172,
              "end_index": 273,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "The process is governed by the Insolvency Act 1986 and the Insolvency (England and Wales) Rules 2016."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              7
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 337,
              "end_index": 590,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "The overall cost of closing or liquidating a limited company in the UK can range from approximately £13 for a simple strike-off to over £6,000, varying significantly based on whether the business is solvent or insolvent and the specific method chosen."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              7,
              8,
              9,
              10,
              11,
              12
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 591,
              "end_index": 729,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "In many instances, directors are not required to pay these costs personally; instead, company assets typically cover the liquidation fees."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              7,
              8
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 786,
              "end_index": 971,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Creditors' Voluntary Liquidation (CVL)**\nThis is the most common route for **insolvent companies** (those unable to pay their debts as they fall due or whose liabilities exceed assets)."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              8,
              13,
              0
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 973,
              "end_index": 1121,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Cost:** A Creditors' Voluntary Liquidation (CVL) typically costs between **£3,000 and £6,000 plus VAT** for relatively straightforward cases"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              7
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 1123,
              "end_index": 1171,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Some sources suggest a range of £4,000-£6,000+"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              14
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 1171,
              "end_index": 1240,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": ", or even £3,000 to £8,000 depending on complexity and asset values"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              7
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 1242,
              "end_index": 1429,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "This figure will increase for more complex scenarios, such as those involving numerous creditors, high-value or overseas assets requiring specialist valuation, or missing company records."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              7,
              9
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 1430,
              "end_index": 1567,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Who Pays:** The fees for a CVL are primarily paid from the **company's assets** once they are realised by the appointed liquidator."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              9,
              12,
              15
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 1568,
              "end_index": 1680,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "If the company lacks sufficient assets to cover the costs, directors may have to personally cover the shortfall."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              8,
              12,
              16
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 1681,
              "end_index": 1838,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Directors who were on the company payroll may be eligible for redundancy pay (which can average £12,000), and this can be used to fund the liquidation fees."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              1,
              17
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 1839,
              "end_index": 2032,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Governing Rule:** The costs are split into pre-appointment (often a fixed fee) and post-appointment stages, with the latter regulated by the **Insolvency (England and Wales) Rules 2016**."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              7,
              8
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 2039,
              "end_index": 2264,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Members' Voluntary Liquidation (MVL)**\nThis route is for **solvent companies** (companies that can pay their debts in full) wishing to close down in a tax-efficient manner, particularly if they hold assets exceeding £25,000."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              8,
              9
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 2266,
              "end_index": 2350,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Cost:** The cost of an MVL typically ranges from **£995 to £4,000 plus VAT**"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              9
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 2352,
              "end_index": 2465,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Some firms offer tiered pricing, with starting costs around £995 + VAT & disbursements for straightforward cases"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              18
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 2467,
              "end_index": 2601,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "More complex MVLs, involving multiple assets, intricate tax planning, or lengthy distribution processes, can cost upwards of £15,000."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              19
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 2602,
              "end_index": 2754,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Who Pays:** The costs of the liquidator must be met, and this is generally agreed upon with the appointed Insolvency Practitioner (IP) in advance."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              7
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 2755,
              "end_index": 2811,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "These costs are usually covered by the company's assets."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              19,
              5
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 2812,
              "end_index": 3002,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Governing Rule:** Directors must sign a statutory declaration of solvency for this process to be used, and the process is governed by the **Insolvency (England and Wales) Rules 2016**."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              0,
              19,
              6
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3009,
              "end_index": 3170,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Compulsory Liquidation**\nThis occurs when a court orders a company to be wound up, often initiated by a creditor who is owed an undisputed debt of £750 or more."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              7
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3172,
              "end_index": 3256,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Cost:** Upfront, the company itself does not directly pay for the liquidation."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              7
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3257,
              "end_index": 3400,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Instead, the **petitioning creditor** is responsible for the initial fees, typically ranging from £3,500 to £4,000 for petitioning the courts"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              0
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3401,
              "end_index": 3438,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "or legal costs starting from £1,500."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              20,
              21,
              22,
              23,
              24,
              25
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3496,
              "end_index": 3660,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "The OR charges a **£6,000 general fee** (set to increase to £7,200 from 9 January 2025) and an additional **15% of assets realised** where they act as liquidator."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              0
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3661,
              "end_index": 3800,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "If a private Insolvency Practitioner is appointed to take over from the OR, their additional fees typically range from £5,000 to £10,000."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              23,
              24
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3801,
              "end_index": 3937,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Who Pays:** The Official Receiver's fees and any subsequent Insolvency Practitioner's fees are paid from the **company's assets**."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              7,
              8
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3938,
              "end_index": 4066,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "The petitioning creditor may attempt to recover their initial costs from the company's assets if sufficient funds are available."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              8,
              19
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4067,
              "end_index": 4269,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Governing Rule:** This process is entirely court-driven, and while directors do not directly pay, it can lead to more stringent investigations into director conduct and potential disqualification."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              23,
              25
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4270,
              "end_index": 4378,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "The **Insolvency Proceedings (Fees) Order 2016** (and its amendments) sets out the Official Receiver's fees."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              8,
              13
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4427,
              "end_index": 4633,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Insolvency Practitioner (IP) Fees:** These are determined based on factors like the complexity of the company's affairs, the number of creditors and employees, and the amount of assets to be realised."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              0,
              14,
              18,
              1,
              17
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4634,
              "end_index": 4737,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Fees can be calculated as a fixed amount, on a time-spent basis, or as a percentage of assets realised."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              14
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4738,
              "end_index": 4802,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "IPs are required to provide comprehensive fee estimates upfront."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              0,
              11,
              2,
              24,
              26
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4803,
              "end_index": 5036,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Priority of Payment:** In a liquidation, the costs and expenses of the liquidation proceedings, including the liquidator's fees, are generally paid first from the realised assets, after any secured creditors with fixed charges."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              11,
              2
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 5037,
              "end_index": 5209,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "This means these costs take precedence over payments to preferential creditors (such as employees and certain HMRC debts), floating charge holders, and unsecured creditors."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              8
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 5210,
              "end_index": 5446,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Other Costs:** Beyond the liquidator's fees, other expenses can include staff redundancy payments, unpaid taxes (HMRC is a creditor), legal and accounting support for disputes, advertising in The Gazette, and statutory bonds/fees."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              3,
              17,
              26
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 5447,
              "end_index": 5640,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Insolvency (England and Wales) Rules 2016:** These rules define what constitutes an insolvency expense and govern the procedures for setting and approving remuneration for office holders."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              3,
              26
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 5641,
              "end_index": 5744,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "For example, Rule 7.108 addresses priority of payment of costs and expenses in compulsory liquidations."
            }
          }
        ],
        "retrieval_metadata": null,
